        "**What to notice:** which clozes changed their candidates, each vector's cosine to its frozen self, and the "
        "reload-parity line.\n\n"
        "<details><summary>Check your reasoning</summary>Not necessarily every cloze. In the CPU build record (revision 602d058, local Windows CPU, pinned torch 2.14.0+cpu, pending a hosted run) `problems` entered the first cloze's top five after adaptation (`applications problems systems phenomena situations`), while the multi-piece gold words `foveation` and `normalization` matched neither before nor after (no single candidate can). The embeddings do all move, because the adapted layers are shared by every input, but only a little: each abstract's adapted vector had a cosine of 0.9466 and 0.9385 to its frozen self. Whether that move helps a similarity task is not measured here. Reload parity held: the ten-record validation perplexity agreed within 1e-6 (10.284235 both ways in that record, revision 602d058), and the candidates and embeddings were identical, so the exported adapter is the model that was evaluated.</details>\n\n"
        "## 10. Your turn — change one thing: fewer trainable layers\n\n"
        "Optional; **Predict → Change → Run → Observe → Explain**. It retrains once, so it takes about as long as one "
        "configuration of the Section 7 grid. It is **exploratory**: it is not part of the pre-registered selection, "
        "so it is compared on validation, and Section 8 does not score the fresh test for it.\n\n"
        "1. **Predict:** with only the last encoder layer trainable instead of four, will the validation "
