        "5. **Explain:** in one sentence, why does training fewer layers change the gain the way it did?\n\n"
        "Set `TRAINABLE_LAYERS_OVERRIDE` back to `0` afterwards to return to the pick.\n\n"
        "<details><summary>Check your reasoning</summary>About 70 % of the validation gain: not all of it, and not zero. In the CPU build record (revision 602d058, local Windows CPU, pinned torch 2.14.0+cpu, pending a hosted run) the default pick (four layers) took validation perplexity from 12.89 to 10.87 (Δ −2.02), and the one-layer re-run went 12.89 → 11.77 → 11.45 (Δ −1.43); its epoch 0 showed the frozen validation perplexity 12.89, the adapter held 16 tensors (28.4 MB instead of 113 MB) and reload parity held (revision 602d058). One layer has a quarter of the four-layer trainable parameters (7,087,872 against 28,351,488; 6.5 % of the 109,514,298 total) and can only re-weight the last layer's view of the text, so it moves the model less in the same number of steps. How much of either gain is specific to this domain is not measured (see Interpretation). If your gain did not shrink, check that epoch 0 showed the frozen validation perplexity; if it did not, the model was not reset (restart and **Run all**).</details>\n\n"
        "## Interpretation and limits\n\n"
        "The frozen encoder already predicts the masked words of paper abstracts far better than a unigram model does (a masked perplexity near 14 against a floor of about a thousand, top-1 accuracy above 50 % against a few percent). A bounded continuation of its own pre-training objective on 300 abstracts, with the configuration chosen on validation by a pre-registered rule (four layers at 5e-5 in the CPU build record), lowers masked perplexity on a fresh test that took no part in any choice by about 2.4 points (14.39 → 11.97 in the CPU build record at revision 602d058, pending a hosted run), with a 113 MB adapter that reloads to the same likelihoods (within 1e-6), candidates and embeddings. That drop combines adaptation to this kind of text with the effect of training on the evaluation's own objective and masking scheme (100 % `[MASK]` at 15 %, where BERT was pretrained with an 80/10/10 mix); no out-of-domain control was run, so how much of it is specific to paper abstracts is not measured. That is the claim: the adaptation contract can continue pre-training end to end on a real corpus, and the number it produces is read against the frozen model and a context-free floor rather than in isolation.\n\n"
        "**What the comparison supports.** The variants are one fixed recipe (AdamW, two epochs, 100 % `[MASK]` "
        "masking at 15 %) at three settings of two knobs, chosen on 50 validation abstracts. The frozen-versus-adapted "
        "comparison isolates one change, continued pre-training of the last layers under this recipe, and it supports "
        "one claim: that change lowers masked perplexity on held-out abstracts of this corpus. It does not separate "
        "adaptation to the domain from adaptation to the masking scheme, it does not show that this recipe beats another adaptation "
        "method, and it does not show that the adapted encoder is more useful for any downstream task.\n\n"
        "**Pretraining overlap.** BERT's pretraining text was BooksCorpus [5] and an English Wikipedia dump of 2018 "
        "or earlier [1]; some SciTLDR-A papers [2] are 2017–2018 OpenReview submissions. Verbatim abstracts in "
        "Wikipedia article text are unlikely but unchecked, so a small overlap cannot be ruled out. It would lower the "
        "frozen perplexity, not the comparison, because the frozen and adapted models are scored on the same records.\n\n"
        "Masked perplexity is intrinsic: it says how well the encoder predicts missing tokens of text it did not write, "
        "at one seeded 15 % masking of one seeded draw of one corpus with no dispersion estimate. It is not embedding "
        "quality, retrieval performance or downstream accuracy, and a lower value does not make the candidates or the "
        "cosine table in Section 9 better — those are observations. The adapter changes the last layers, which every "
        "input shares, so every embedding shifts (Section 9 prints each vector's cosine to its frozen self) and the "
        "fill-mask `score` stays a softmax ranking signal, not a probability. Text is lower-cased and accent-stripped by "
        "the tokenizer; texts over 512 WordPiece tokens are rejected everywhere, never truncated; the checkpoint carries "
        "the gender and occupation associations the upstream card documents, and continued pre-training on a corpus does "
        "not remove them.\n\n"
        "Three things to carry to real data. **Floors first:** the unigram floor and the frozen masked perplexity on "
        "*your* held-out documents are the numbers to read before any adapted one. **Leakage and selection:** "
        "de-duplicate texts across splits (the contract does this case-insensitively), split by document collection or "
        "author when your documents come from one, and choose every setting on validation, never on the documents you "
        "report. **Downstream:** a better masked perplexity on your domain is a reason to *measure* "
        "your similarity or classification task with the adapted encoder, not evidence that it improved.\n\n"
        "Successful execution proves that the recorded repository revision's pipeline modules, carried in this standalone "
        "notebook, can acquire and digest-verify the pinned model snapshot, fetch and digest-verify a real corpus, validate "
        "the demonstrated dataset contract without leakage, execute both inference contracts, select a configuration on "
        "validation by a pre-registered rule and run a bounded continued pre-training, evaluate it under the pre-registered settings by masked-token "
        "metrics against a trivial floor and the frozen model on a fresh test that took no part in any choice, and emit "
        "the shown machine-readable artifacts — without the repository being reachable. It does **not** "
        "establish benchmark superiority, embedding or cloze quality on any domain, a usable acceptance threshold, or "
        "production fitness.\n\n"
