        "## Glossary\n\n"
        "- **`[MASK]` / cloze:** the special token that hides a word, and a sentence with one word hidden for the "
        "model to fill.\n"
        "- **WordPiece:** BERT's tokenizer; it splits rare words into several pieces, so one word can be several "
        "tokens.\n"
        "- **Softmax score:** the model's scores over all 30,522 tokens turned into numbers that sum to one; a ranking "
        "signal, not a calibrated probability of being right.\n"
        "- **Masked perplexity:** the exponential of the average negative log-likelihood of the hidden tokens; lower "
        "is better, and a value of *k* means the model is on average as unsure as a uniform choice among *k* tokens. It "
        "is token-weighted over WordPiece pieces (`##` continuation pieces, often easy to guess from their neighbours, "
        "count like whole words), it is comparable only between models scored on the same records under the same "
        "`MASK_RATE` and `SEED`, and it is not comparable with a causal language model's perplexity or with "
        "pseudo-log-likelihood scores.\n"
        "- **Bits per masked token:** the same average expressed in bits.\n"
        "- **Top-1 / top-5 accuracy:** the share of hidden tokens that are the model's first choice / among its first "
        "five.\n"
        "- **Unigram floor:** a model that predicts every hidden token from word frequencies alone, ignoring the "
        "context; the score any useful model must beat.\n"
        "- **Continued pre-training:** further training on the model's own masked-word objective, with a new domain's "
        "unlabelled text.\n"
        "- **Trainable layers:** the encoder layers whose weights training may change; the rest stay frozen.\n"
        "- **Epoch / validation selection:** one pass over the training documents; the epoch kept is the one with the "
        "lowest validation perplexity.\n"
        "- **Pre-registration:** writing the candidate settings and the rule that picks among them down before any of "
        "them runs, so the result cannot steer the choice.\n"
        "- **Training / validation / test split:** documents used to train, to choose the configuration and the "
        "epoch, and to report the final result under the settings fixed in advance.\n"
        "- **Exposed development test:** a split that has already influenced a choice, so its numbers can be optimistic; "
        "it is reported with that label, never as the held-out result.\n"
        "- **Embedding / pooling / cosine:** a fixed-length vector for a text, how the per-token vectors are combined "
        "into it (`cls` or `mean`), and the similarity of two unit vectors (1 = same direction).\n"
        "- **Adapter / reload parity:** the saved trained layers, and the check that a pipeline rebuilt from them gives "
        "the same perplexity (within 1e-6), candidates and embeddings.\n\n"
